<title>SWITZERLAND: TABLE-Baer H1 net profit up 62 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Baer H1 net profit up 62 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>				   (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net			109.7	     vs 67.7</p>
<p> Minority interests	   2.2		 vs 1.1</p>
<p> Net after min		  107.5	     vs 66.5</p>
<p> Gross profit		   175.4	     vs 102.7</p>
<p> Assets under mgt (billions)78.3		vs 56.2</p>
<p> Net interest income	  61.6		vs 56.0</p>
<p> Commissions, service fees  216.1	     vs 148.7</p>
<p> Trading			  129.0	     vs 79.1</p>
<p> Net operating income	 419.3	     vs 293.2</p>
<p> Operating expenses	   243.9	     vs 190.4</p>
<p>  - personnel costs	   152.2	     vs 119.4</p>
<p> Taxes			    45.9		vs 18.2</p>
<p> Cash flow			129.5	     vs 84.5</p>
<p> Earnings per bearer share  91.2 Sfr	  vs 56.5 Sfr</p>
<p> Total assets (vs 31.12.96) 14,530.1	  vs 9,990.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Swiss private banking group Julius Baer Holding is home to Bank Julius Baer.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
